Make the catalog's sets of tables and schemas safe under concurrency.

One set of tables per schema is shared by every connection to the DuckDB.
Binding a statement replaces a table's entry in it under the set's lock; a
listing walks it under the lock and reads what it found afterwards; and a
rename's or drop's commit erased from it without the lock. So an erase beside
a bind or a walk corrupted the set, and a bind between a listing's walks freed
entries the listing was still reading (the transaction kept only the latest
entry of each table): the process segfaulted, or a later listing looped
forever. And the set's lock was held over each request to the catalog: a
bind loaded its table, and a listing asked for the schema's tables, under
it, so the binds of one schema's tables queued behind each other's round
trips. Now:

- Erases (a drop's or rename's commit) find and erase under the set's lock.
- A transaction keeps every entry it looked up or listed alive until it ends
  (IcebergTransaction::KeepAlive, HoldTable), so an entry lives as long as
  anything holds it, whatever the set does meanwhile.
- A listing walks a copy of the set taken under the lock.
- A bind loads its table into an entry of its own without the lock and then
  puts it in the set under it; a listing asks the catalog for the schema's
  tables without it and merges them under it, leaving out a name the set
  erased since it asked, which the catalog may no longer have.
- A transaction's requests to the catalog, which share its connection's one
  HTTP client, run one at a time (IcebergTransaction::catalog_requests), and
  its hold on its tables is under its lock: a listing's scans of several
  schemas run on DuckDB's threads at once.
- A rename the catalog committed replaces an entry the set already has under
  the new name (one a listing of the catalog put there after the commit)
  rather than fail a rename that happened: the catalog, which refuses a
  rename onto an existing table, decides.
- The schema set takes its lock for every access, and keeps a removed schema,
  whose table set others may still be reading, until the catalog is
  detached; iceberg_to_ducklake walks copies of both sets.

